#: source/store/types/local-store.md:1
msgid "Local Store"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:3
msgid "**Store URL format**: `local`, _root_"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:5
msgid ""
"This store type accesses a Nix store in the local filesystem directly (i.e. "
"not via the Nix daemon). _root_ is an absolute path that is prefixed to "
"other directories such as the Nix store directory. The store pseudo-URL "
"`local` denotes a store that uses `/` as its root directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:11
msgid "Local chroot store"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:13
msgid ""
"A local store that uses a _root_ other than `/` is called a _local chroot "
"store_. With such stores, the store directory is \"logically\" still `/nix/"
"store`, so programs stored in them can only be built and executed by "
"`chroot`\\-ing into _root_. Chroot stores only support building and running "
"on Linux when [`mount namespaces`](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/"
"mount_namespaces.7.html) and [`user namespaces`](https://man7.org/linux/man-"
"pages/man7/user_namespaces.7.html) are enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:20
msgid ""
"For example, the following uses `/tmp/root` as the chroot environment to "
"build or download `nixpkgs#hello` and then execute it:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:28
msgid ""
"Here, the \"physical\" store location is `/tmp/root/nix/store`, and Nix's "
"store metadata is in `/tmp/root/nix/var/nix/db`."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:31
msgid ""
"It is also possible, but not recommended, to change the \"logical\" location "
"of the Nix store from its default of `/nix/store`. This makes it impossible "
"to use default substituters such as `https://cache.nixos.org/`, and thus you "
"may have to build everything locally. Here is an example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:41
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:43
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-local-store-build-dir\">[`build-dir`](#store-local-store-"
"build-dir)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:45
msgid ""
"The directory on the host, in which derivations' temporary build directories "
"are created."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:47
msgid ""
"If not set, Nix will use the `builds` subdirectory of its configured state "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:49
msgid ""
"Note that builds are often performed by the Nix daemon, so its `build-dir` "
"applies."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:51
msgid ""
"Nix will create this directory automatically with suitable permissions if it "
"does not exist. Otherwise its permissions must allow all users to traverse "
"the directory (i.e. it must have `o+x` set, in unix parlance) for non-"
"sandboxed builds to work correctly."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:54
msgid ""
"This is also the location where [`--keep-failed`](../../command-ref/opt-"
"common.md#opt-keep-failed) leaves its files."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:56
msgid ""
"If Nix runs without sandbox, or if the platform does not support sandboxing "
"with bind mounts (e.g. macOS), then the [`builder`](../../language/"
"derivations.md#attr-builder)'s environment will contain this directory, "
"instead of the virtual location [`sandbox-build-dir`](../../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-sandbox-build-dir)."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:58 source/store/types/local-store.md:70
#: source/store/types/local-store.md:185
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:60
msgid ""
"`build-dir` must not be set to a world-writable directory. Placing temporary "
"build directories in a world-writable place allows other users to access or "
"modify build data that is currently in use. This alone is merely an "
"impurity, but combined with another factor this has allowed malicious "
"derivations to escape the build sandbox."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:64
msgid ""
"See also the global [`build-dir`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-build-"
"dir) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/local-store.md:66 source/store/types/local-store.md:146
msgid "**Default:** \\``"
msgstr ""

